### Use with an HTTP client that supports .http files (for example, REST Client).
### Set the password locally. Do not commit real values or paste tokens into Git.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:3000
@username = demo
@password = REPLACE_LOCALLY_WITH_YOUR_AUTH_PASSWORD

### Connection readiness (no token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Login — the following requests use this response's token
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Create a fictional order (PT input, EN stored output)
POST {{baseUrl}}/order
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "numeroPedido": "v10089015vdb-01",
  "valorTotal": 10000,
  "dataCriacao": "2023-07-19T12:24:11.529Z",
  "items": [{ "idItem": "2434", "quantidadeItem": 1, "valorItem": 1000 }]
}

### List
GET {{baseUrl}}/order/list
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Read
GET {{baseUrl}}/order/v10089015vdb-01
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Partial update (EN input; identifier remains unchanged)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/order/v10089015vdb-01
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "value": 50000 }

### Delete only the fictional order above
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/order/v10089015vdb-01
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
